        "evidence": "claim permits decisions only when remaining assignments support them; probe advances with total lower bound >=4 and all slice lower bounds >=-2, and otherwise retains uncertainty unless upper bounds prove rejection. prediction contrasts this with fixed slice-stratified review using corrected point totals: residual uncertainty can make a point decision unsupported. Matched copies, identical withheld rows, logged attempts, sixteen successful adjudications and seventy minutes supply a feasible proposed discriminator. assumptions keep unflagged-label status and implementation capacity visible, with unresolved fallback; no observed advantage is asserted. Bounds imply the proposed safety mechanism by inference. Archive B-688d75e2b2ff62cd4f9d supplies the same decision-under-unresolved-labels relation."
